# React Component Conventions

## Structure & Naming

- Use **functional components** exclusively — no class components.
- Name components in **PascalCase**; files match the component name (e.g., `UserCard.tsx`).
- One component per file; co-locate subcomponents only when they are not reused elsewhere.
- Keep components focused: if JSX exceeds ~80 lines, extract into smaller components.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
export default function user_card({ name }: any) { ... }

// ✅ GOOD
interface UserCardProps { name: string; avatarUrl?: string }
export function UserCard({ name, avatarUrl }: UserCardProps) { ... }
```

## Styling

- Prefer **CSS Modules** (`Component.module.css`) or a utility-first library (e.g., Tailwind).
- Avoid inline `style` objects except for dynamic values that cannot be expressed in CSS.
- Never hardcode colors or spacing — use design tokens / CSS variables.
